> asymptotes (x^2+1)/(x-1)
asymptotes of (x^2 + 1)/(x - 1):
  vertical: x = 1 (f -> -inf from the left, +inf from the right)
  oblique: y = x + 1 as x -> ±inf
  proved symbolically: f = N/D with deg N = 2, deg D = 1; poles are the real roots of D that are roots of N of lower multiplicity (others are holes); at infinity the quotient of N by D
> zeros x^3 - x
zeros of x^3 - x:
  3 zeros:
    x = -1
    x = 0
    x = 1
  proved: a polynomial of degree 3 has 3 roots counted with multiplicity
